  "question": {
    "text": "Bag 1 contains 4 white balls and 5 black balls, and Bag 2 contains $n$ white balls and 3 black balls. One ball is drawn randomly from Bag 1 and transferred to Bag 2. A ball is then drawn randomly from Bag 2. If the probability, that the ball drawn is white, is $29 / 45$, then $n$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3iFPN",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "fNF8l",
      "text": "3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bHn80",
      "text": "5",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IcJsZ",
      "text": "4",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Bag $1 \\rightarrow 4 w, 5 B$\nBag $2 \\rightarrow n w, 3 B$\n$(\\mathrm{I}) \\rightarrow$ Transferred ball is white $P(w)=\\frac{n+1}{n+4} \\cdot \\frac{4}{9}$\n(II) $\\rightarrow$ Transferred ball is black $P(w)=\\frac{5}{9} \\cdot \\frac{n}{n+4}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{4 n+4}{9 n+36}+\\frac{5 n}{9 n+36}=\\frac{29}{45} \\\\\n& \\frac{9 n+4}{9 n+36}=\\frac{29}{45} \\Rightarrow n=6\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
